{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T17:52:51.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b76020648d06f21575f92b8e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1du7s3","claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-1du7s3","lineage:pm-4of199","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-1du7s3+pm-wlxf8f+pm-y26mvc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1du7s3","claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-1du7s3","lineage:pm-4of199","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T17:52:51.175Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-07T17:52:51.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implemented on branch fix/cli-option-contract-truthfulness. assertNoSwallowedAnnotationOption (src/cli/register-annotations.ts) runs right after the transposed-subcommand check and before every source-count check, for every text alias of comments, notes and learnings. It throws createFlagLikeAnnotationValueRefusal (src/sdk/annotations.ts), which names a swallowed --file or --stdin in its own form (\"drop --add and pass --file <path> on its own\") and, for --stdin or --file=<path> followed by an operand, names the operand that cannot be combined with it. A retry is offered only when dropping the text flag leaves exactly one source; the CLI recovery repair (src/cli/runtime/annotation-option-retry.ts, wired in repairInvocationRecovery and excluded from message-text inference) rewrites it as the typed argv minus the text flag, so tracker scope, --message, --author and --json stay, and withdraws it when the argv holds zero or two swallowing pairs. Direct SDK callers get the same source-form guidance with placeholder examples.\n\nVerification: the built-CLI spec runs the prescribed suggested_retry_args for comments, notes and learnings and each one appends the file text; it also covers --add --stdin x (named operand, no retry) and --add --stdin (retry run with piped stdin). The in-process spec covers every branch, with a negative control that disables the check (vi.doMock) and gets the old \"positional [text] or with --add\" message back. The unit spec for the repair covers rewrite, attached --add=--file, withdrawal (no pair, two pairs, after --, no command token) and pass-through. The full suite passed 12,202 of 12,203; the one failure was a host npm-path issue in an unrelated spec, and it passes with NODE_PATH set.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"e7232799fc05cde38281e7f164c47d5071e515a010205a823b6bca410ad1084f","after_hash":"5b672904228d2ae03228843737c42d1f81545a947dfe6aa2c2f0ef11e451d0e6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"248094ea5d66b0e3e9bee0a79f80a8c40251e63abb6e1805433679d9576a91ca"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T18:21:53.911Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b76020648d06f21575f92b8e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1du7s3","claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-1du7s3","lineage:pm-4of199","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-1du7s3+pm-wlxf8f+pm-y26mvc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1du7s3","claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-1du7s3","lineage:pm-4of199","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T18:21:53.910Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 found two retry gaps here, both fixed in commit c6210382d. (1) P1: pm item comments --add --file pm-one pm-two parses id=pm-one with text pm-two, but dropping --add yields --file pm-one pm-two, which would read the file pm-one into item pm-two. The repair now requires the producer's intended option and operand at the rewritten position and withdraws the retry otherwise. (2) An earlier --add hello (overwritten by Commander), another text alias, or --add-json made the retry a two-source invocation. The producer now offers no retry when another alias or --add-json is present, and the repair withdraws when the text flag appears again in the argv.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T18:21:53.911Z"}],"before_hash":"5b672904228d2ae03228843737c42d1f81545a947dfe6aa2c2f0ef11e451d0e6","after_hash":"6b5c16684d33159b54470d1a15a9e62d1abb4088c2230fa240cd0ab9ad1d3ffc","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f6a5763466dcbf0f546c8e623851f401dab8b9bd59d9ecbfab47bcc84e609ac8"}
